      "side": 1,
      "message": "Firas, you will bump into many problems like that during Zephyr development. You need to get more familiar with Zephyr APIs. General approach is that you check a description of a used function in a [header file](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/include/zephyr/drivers/gpio.h) and see what argument it takes. You can also check a previous argument  - [GPIO_INT_EDGE_TO_ACTIVE](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/include/zephyr/drivers/gpio.h#L203) and see what are other alternatives. In this case, you probably want to use `GPIO_INT_EDGE_TO_INACTIVE` to enable interrupt, edge to inactive, if it is what CrosEC driver does.",
